---
description: Never add per-type switches/maps that must grow when a new item type is added
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

# Open/closed for item types — no per-type extension points outside viewers/editors

Adding a new form item type (e.g. `"field" | "heading" | "panel" | "…"`) must
**not** require editing shared helpers, orchestrators, or rename/clone utilities.

The **only** places that may know concrete type names are:

1. **Viewers** — per-type render entries in a `Viewers` bag
2. **Editors** — per-type editor entries (and host wrappers like `wrapWithRequired`)

Everything else must stay open via **generics** constrained by shared structure
(e.g. `Params extends ParamsDom<TypeNames, { name: string }>`), not by switching
on `"field" | "heading" | …`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — must be updated for every new type (OCP violation)
const withItemName = (item: SomeFormItem<TypeNames, Params>, name: string) => {
  switch (item.type) {
    case "field":
      return { ...item, params: { ...item.params, name } };
    case "heading":
      return { ...item, params: { ...item.params, name } };
    case "panel":
      return { ...item, params: { ...item.params, name } };
  }
};

// ✅ GOOD — open for any TypeNames; shared `name` is the constraint
const withItemName = <
  TypeNames extends string,
  Params extends ParamsDom<TypeNames, { name: string }>,
>(
  item: SomeFormItem<TypeNames, Params>,
  name: string,
): SomeFormItem<TypeNames, Params> => ({
  ...item,
  params: { ...item.params, name },
});
```

## Also forbidden

- `Record<TypeNames, …>` / `if (type === "field")` helpers outside viewers/editors
- “Utility” maps that list every type just to do a shared-field update
- Casting around a union spread instead of fixing the generic

Same idea as `cloneFlatItems`: operate on the common shape; let viewers/editors
own type-specific UI.
